  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up use of Safe Delivery App (SDA) for provision of care for maternal and new-born health in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a scale up in the use of Safe Delivery App (SDA) in Tanzania. This project will complement Government of Tanzania&#x2019;s efforts to improve skills and knowledge of health care workers in order to provide good quality of health care services to mothers and new-born babies. Ifakara Health Institute will coordinate with regional health directors in order to secure ownership at local level. The SDA is a job aid that provides necessary competences for a respectful, evidence-based Basic Emergency Maternal, Obstetric and Neonatal Care (BEMONC) for women in labour that adheres to WHO and national guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
